From 15e0f8a27cf9ea023ef81fe9dc39020b30eaa87b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:35:34 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ecash: retain experimental static-package block construction
 candidate

Replace fee-index/direct-parent selection with a snapshot, ancestor-package
accounting and dependency-ordered selection. The intent was to avoid repeated
ancestor-score updates while preserving parent-before-child construction.

This is an experimental historical candidate, not a validated optimization.
The current payload has stale size, sigcheck and fee accounting and diamond
double counting. Its claimed O(n log n) bound is not established. The pinned
ABC build fails three existing mining assertions; BCHN needs a reviewed port.
Keep it out of the default series. Metadata recovery does not repair its code.

Metadata-backfill: This explanation and envelope are newly written; they do
not claim recovery of a lost per-patch message or its original author/date.
The source diff bytes are unchanged. Recorded port/import commit:
578bbcddd210de1601b280967700e07420f23782 (Lotus monorepo).
Historical lineage: import 9686d09aac0ebe58d4ad173b2fb12360776869de
references schancel/bitcoin-abc simple-mining (D2866). That branch currently
ends at c1bdbe00d29042af81e1846728088f32867c3498, whose original subject is
"WIP: Stupidly simple mining." The modern port is not that historical diff.

Validation: exact raw-diff and mailbox replays produce the same source tree.
See daemon/docs/ecash-block-assembly-review.md and support-matrix.md for
behavioral evidence and applicability limits; no new build is asserted here.

